ncies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot v4.8 master\n- Probably since it was added in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122352 (cc @Repiteo )\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors (2400x1350 @ 60.00 Hz, 1920x1080 @ 60.00 Hz) - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2070 (NVIDIA; 32.0.16.1088) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-10750H CPU @ 2.60GHz (12 threads) - 15.82 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nRunning the `[MethodBind] check bound enums` test case by itself fails:\n`./bin/godot.windows.editor.dev.x86_64.exe --test --tc=\"[MethodBind] check bound enums\"`\n```\n[doctest] doctest version is \"2.4.12\"\n[doctest] run with \"--help\" for options\n===============================================================================\nC:\\Projects\\godotsrc\\godot\\tests//core/object/test_method_bind.cpp(223):\nTEST CASE:  [MethodBind] check bound enums\n\nC:\\Projects\\godotsrc\\godot\\tests//core/object/test_method_bind.cpp(233): ERROR: CHECK( member ) is NOT correct!\n  values: CHECK( nullptr )\n\nC:\\Projects\\godotsrc\\godot\\tests//core/object/test_method_bind.cpp(223): FATAL ERROR: test case CRASHED: SIGSEGV - Segmentation violation signal\n\n===============================================================================\n[doctest] test cases: 1 | 0 passed | 1 failed | 1423 skipped\n[doctest] assertions: 1 | 0 passed | 1 failed |\n[doctest] Status: FAILURE!\n```\n\nRunning with other tests works fine ` --test --tc=\"[MethodBind]*\"`, so it must be depending on the results of another test. It should be self contained.\nI think its because `MethodBindTester` never gets created.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nRun this single test case: ` --test --tc=\"[MethodBind] check bound enums\"`\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ND